    \textit{Example for Reporting to Protection Layer.} After the last update of flow $e_2$, as shown in Figure \ref{pl}, it reaches the overflow value of counter $p$. It is, therefore reported to the Protection Layer with initial information $\langle ID_{e_2},0,1 \rangle$. On the other hand, flow \(e_5\) comes and makes the counter $f$ to be 256. Thus, it reports an overflow of counter $f$. Upon reporting, its information in the Protection Layer updates to $\langle FP_{e_5},4,3\rangle$, satisfying the pruning condition \(f_{of} > p_{of}\). As a result, its information is cleared from both layers.

