ProMis obtains a probability for each coordinate $(x_i, y_i)$ via Hybrid ProbLog~\cite{HybridProbLog}.
Using a stochastic error model~\cite{flade2021error}, it converts crowdsourced geographic features from OpenStreetMap into probabilistic facts.
These probabilistic facts encode probabilities for spatial relations between coordinates and tagged features, e.g., whether a coordinate is likely over a public park or far away from the nearest sports arena.
