\begin{lemma}\label{lem:QRATA}
	Suppose we have a DQBF: $\forall U \exists E \phi$.
	Let $l$ be a literal of some existential variable in $E$ and $C$ be a clause not in $\phi$, where $C$ contains literal $l$.

	With respect to existential literal/variable $l$, recall the DQBF definition of an outer clause $O_K$ of some clause $K$, according to Definition~\ref{def:O}.
	% $\bigvee_{x\in K,\var(x)\neq \var(l) }^{\var(x)\in \exists ,D_{\var(x)}\subset D_{\var(l)}} x \vee\bigvee_{x\in D_{\var(l)}} x$.
	If for every clause $D\in \phi$ with $\bar l \in D$ satisfies:
	$\phi \wedge \bar C \wedge \bar O_D \wedge \bar l \vdash_1 \bot$,
