Instead of p-simulating EUR and QRATU separately, what we will show here is a simulation of a powerful mixed reduction rule that acts like a combination of QRATU and EUR and even works for DQBF. QRATU and EUR will both be special cases when the prefix gives a QBF. %QRATU requires $\phi \wedge \bar C \wedge \bar O_D \vdash_1 \bot$ for every  $D\in \phi$ with $\bar u \in D$ which always covers the condition regardless of reachability of resolution paths. EUR requires no unit propagation checks because when EUR is applied there is no $D\in \epsilon$ with $\bar u \in D$.

\begin{lemma}\label{lem:mixedred}
	Suppose we have a DQBF: $\forall U \exists E \psi$.	
	Let $u$ be a literal of some universal variable in $U$ and $C \vee u$ be a clause in $\psi$, i.e $\psi=\phi\wedge (C\vee u)$.
	Recall Definition~\ref{def:O} for the definition of $\mathcal{S}$
	%Let $\mathcal{S}= \{x \in E \mid \var(u) \in D_x\}$ be the set of existential variables that depend on $u$. Let $\mathcal{A}= \bigcap_{s\in S} D_s \setminus \{\var(u)\}$ be the set of universal variables that appear in the dependency set $D_s$ of every variable $s\in \mathcal{S}$, except for $u$.
	Let $\chi_0=\pathc(\psi, C\vee u, \mathcal{S})$, the set of clauses reachable from $C\vee u$ via resolution path in $\mathcal{S}$. %With respect to universal variable $u$, define the outer clause $O_K$ of some clause $K$ to be $\bigvee_{l\in K, \var(l)\in \exists}^{\var(l) \notin \mathcal{S}, D_{\var(l)}\subset \mathcal{A} } l \vee\bigvee_{l\in K}^{\var(l)\in \mathcal{A}} l$. 

	If for every clause $D\in \chi_0$ with $\bar u \in D$ satisfies:
	$\phi \wedge \bar C \wedge \bar O_D \vdash_1 \bot$,
	then using a polynomial bounded (in the size of $\forall U \exists E \psi$) number of rules of \dFrege we can extend $\exists E$ to $\exists E'$, which includes for every variable $x$ in $\mathcal{S}$ a variable $x'$ such that  $D_{x'}\subseteq D_x$ and derive the clauses of $(\phi \wedge C)'$ which is a copy of $\phi\wedge C$ where every $x$ in $\mathcal{S}$ is replaced by $x'$.

\end{lemma}


As specified in the lemma the proof is done by replacing literals with different extension variables. The origins of the replacement scheme used here trace back to the simulation of QRAT by \Gfull~\cite{CH22}, although this simulation here simulates a more powerful rule and works in the DQBF setting. This is despite being seemingly handicapped by only being able to create definitions that are existential variables, whereas \Gfull can use complicated functions to witness universal variables. To overcome this we hide functions that previously witness universal variables into new definitions of the existential variables that depend on them. 

%In this definition, the outer universal variables have to be in the dependency set of all members of $\mathcal{S}$, likewise existential variables cannot have dependencies outside of these outer universal variables. This will ensure the modification of Skolem functions used in QRATU's soundness does not add new dependencies.

