\subsection{P-simulation of the Sequent Calculus}\label{sec:G}
Let $\Gamma$ and $\Delta$ each be sets of logical formulas. A \emph{sequent} $\Gamma \vdash \Delta$ expresses that any Boolean assignment to the free variables that satisfies every formula in $\Gamma$ also satisfies at least one formula in $\Delta$. A \emph{sequent calculus} is a proof system that uses sequents as lines. There are different sequent calculi, and sequent calculi can work for different logics. The QBF sequent calculus we are interested in is \Gfull, because of its position the the proof system hierarchy near the top (Figure~\ref{fig:QBFsimstruct}).


