We next analyze the impact of our most critical design decisions.
All variants have been trained the same number of epochs with the full \dataset{DuMaS} dataset unless otherwise stated. Our full model includes the DINOv2 image encoder, multi-resolution feature aggregation (Multi-res., \cref{subsubsec:multires}), and multiple query sampling (Multi-sampl., \cref{subsubsec:multisampling}). 

%
\begin{figure*}
 \centering
 \includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{figures/results/ablations_combined1.pdf}
  \caption{\textbf{Ablations.} We ablate parts of our method (multi-resolution and multi-sampling, respectively) \new{on two challenging examples containing thin structures (net and zebra stripes) and albedo entanglement (net has a similar albedo to the white parts of the basketball, in front of a patterned background).}
  }
 \label{fig:ablations}
