\end{figure}


In contrast, there exists a family of simple~$3$-planar graphs with~$5.5n-15$ edges whose standard drawings have~$5.5n-21$ crossings (\cref{fig:tightness_3}).
Thus, there is a gap of~$1.1n$ between the lower and the upper bound for the crossing number of~$3$-plane drawings.

