Before proving Theorem~\ref{thm:tightness} we state some technical results first.
In what follows we denote $\calP(y,k)=\sum_{j=0}^{k}e^{-y}y^{j}/j!$ the probability that that a random variable distributed according to a Poisson of mean $y$ is at most $k$.
