Table \ref{fig:full_function_vs_code_chunk}(a) compares the performance of the Full Function and Code Chunk approaches on Dataset 1. The Code Chunk method significantly outperforms the Full Function approach across all metrics. It improves accuracy by ~53.9\%, precision by ~42.8\%, recall by ~35.5\%, and F1-score by ~42.0\%. We also gets the same kinds of results on Dataset 2 in figure \ref{fig:full_function_vs_code_chunk}(b). In this case our proposed code chunk based model improves accuracy by 35.22\%, precision by 28.16\%, recall by 35.59\% and F1-score by 32.26\%. 
