\myparagraph{Results and discussion.} %
The results, summarized in \tblref{simple:passage}, show the
super-linear improvement of using additional threads in high-variance
motion planning problems. The high variance phenomena is also apparent
in the high failure rate ($33\%$) of the single thread method (i.e., the
runtime exceeded 3000 seconds in a single try).

The remarkable advantage of the different restarting strategies over
the parallel-OR model is also evident, with the slowest restarting
strategy (wide search) giving an average runtime almost $5$ times
faster than that of the parallel strategy. The large variance and gap
between the min and the max in \tblref{simple:passage} are further
evidence of the high variance.

