        \item Case 1: This case represents transformations where the value in the input data is altered, such as converting data formats (e.g., from CSV to Flat Buffers), while the key remains unchanged. Data compression also falls under this case.

        \item Case 2: This case represents transformations that involve data cleansing, where both the key and the value may be modified (e.g., correcting key-value pairs or standardizing data).
