\end{center}
 {\tt iprof}  allows filtering events, choosing tracing modes, turning on or off features such as hardware telemetry, and specifying parsing and analysis types for the collected traces according to the user's needs. Once the LTTng Traces collected, the Babeltrace2 library reads the CFT reader and Muxer plugin for serializing messages by time, and then he custom plugins then generate the desired views of the trace.




