\subsection{On-node Processing}
\vspace{-5pt}
Users can choose to save only the aggregate of the trace, which is lightweight, typically in the range of kilobytes, depending on storage availability and usage requirements. These aggregates can be replayed to generate tally profiles and are the default setting for multi-node experiments. In such scenarios, each local master sends its aggregate to the global master, where the summaries are combined into a composite profile. Traces are temporarily stored in local scratchpad memory to generate these aggregates. For detailed postmortem analysis, users can enable the {\tt --trace} option to permanently save the LTTng trace for one or more specific ranks. We have experimented this on a production machine and successfully scaled up to 512 nodes run.
