This section provides the outline of a general framework for deriving a reproducible version of any traditional Krylov subspace method. 
The framework is based on two main concepts: 1) identifying the issues caused by parallelization and, hence, the  non-associativity of floating-point computations; 2) carefully mitigating these issues primarily with the help of computer arithmetic techniques as well as programming guidelines. 
The framework was implicitly used for the derivation of the reproducible variants of the Preconditioned Conjugate Gradient (PCG) method~\cite{iakymchuk20ijhpca,iakymchuk19jcam}. %The framework is illustrated by its application to the PCG method.

