\begin{abstract}
    The geometric dimension of a Vector Addition System with States (VASS), emerged in Leroux and Schmitz (2019) and
    formalized by Fu, Yang, and Zheng (2024), quantifies the dimension of the vector space spanned by cycle effects in
    the system. This paper explores the VASS reachability problem through the lens of geometric dimension, revealing key
    differences from the traditional dimensional parameterization. Notably, we establish that the reachability problem
    for both geometrically 1-dimensional and 2-dimensional VASS is \textsf{PSPACE}-complete, achieved by extending the
    pumping technique originally proposed by Czerwi\'nski et al.\ (2019).
\end{abstract}

