When the KL divergence is the target metric and the underlying covariance matrix is singular, we define a trace-based proxy for the KL divergence using Subblock SLQ, which is computable from small principal submatrices. This formulation remains well-defined even when the covariance matrix is singular. Lemma~\ref{thm:fullrank} shows that principal submatrices can retain full rank as long as their size does not exceed the rank of the full matrix, ensuring that the proxy KL divergence remains stable and tractable in regimes where the classical KL is undefined.

