\section{Experimental Results}
\label{results}
\subsection{Characterization Experiments}
\vspace{-0.5em}
\subsubsection{Torque and Bandwidth} We placed a Vernier Go Direct Force and Acceleration Sensor 70 mm away from the pivot point to measure the force the \textit{DexWrist} could exert. The rated torque output was calculated to be 3.75$\pm$0.05 Nm (10 trials were collected for all experiments). We simultaneously calculated the bandwidth using the rising time ($t_r$), the time taken to reach 90\% torque from 10\% torque, with the $B (Hz) = 0.35/t_r (s)$ relationship. The resulting bandwidth is 10.15$\pm$1.34 Hz, which is on the lower end of the desired range.

\subsubsection{Back-driveability Torque} In a similar setup as before, the Vernier Go Direct Force and Acceleration Sensor was used to measure the force required to back-drive the \textit{DexWrist} as the wrist was lowered onto the sensor. The torque necessary to back-drive the robotic wrist is 0.33$\pm$0.06 Nm.

\subsubsection{Load Capacity} To validate the strength of the \textit{DexWrist}, the Vernier Go Direct Force and Acceleration Sensor was used to push against the wrist hard stops with force equivalent to 5 kg. The structural skeleton of the wrist was able to sustain the required load capacity without damage.

\subsubsection{Speed, Angular Precision, and Range of Motion} We recorded the end effector motion of the \textit{DexWrist} when moved between its motion limits.  The Vernier Video Analysis software was used to track the end effector and calculate its speed, final position, and range of motion. The resulting rated speed greatly surpassed our requirements at $96.6\pm9.4$ RPM, the angular precision was 1.65 degrees, and the range of motion for both F/E and R/U were confirmed to be -40 to 40 degrees.

\subsubsection{Size and Weight} The \textit{DexWrist} length fits within the designated requirements. Due to the spherical bearings necessary for the driving links, the height and width were above the required size. However, the width is only 4\% larger than the target value. The assembly weighs 0.97 kg.

