Results expressed in the HH:MM time format reveal an easily discernible pattern. As expected, each addition of a security measure leads to an increase in execution time. 
However, while for SGX it is possible to state that a fully encrypted FL pipeline doubles the execution time, TDX adds only a slight overhead to the wall-clock time.

Since our approach is not affected by loss in learning performance, as we perform a standard training routine as in~\cite{casella2024analysis}, and due to space constraints, we omit plots and discussion about model's accuracies.

To better understand the overhead added by each single mechanism, we reproduced the performance model presented in~\cite{casella2024analysis}. The execution time $T$ can be seen as a linear combination with one term to capture the relationship with each discussed security mechanism:
