 We work with the sequence of the Fourier coefficients of $v^k(z, \cdot)$ in the angular variable $\theta=(\cos\varphi,\sin\varphi)$, 
\begin{align}\label{eq:vkn}
	v^k_n(z)=\frac{1}{2\pi} \int_{-\pi}^{\pi} v^k(z,\theta ) e^{-i n\varphi}d\varphi, \quad k=0,1, \;n \in \Z.
\end{align}
The upper index $k$ denotes the level of the flux, while the lower index $n$ is the Fourier coefficient in the angular variable.

In terms of the Cauchy Riemann operators $\partial = (\partial_{x} - i\partial_{y})/2$ and
$\overline{\partial} = (\partial_{x} + i\partial_{y})/2$,
the advection operator becomes $\theta \cdot\nabla_z = e^{-i\varphi}\overline{\partial} + e^{i\varphi}\partial$.
