It is observed that the reconstruction near the boundary is unstable since the
singular integral equation amplifies the error.
We can say that concentration of errors near the boundary is expected due to
theoretical evaluation of numerical integration. Although the integral is not
singular, it is numerically singular near the end of the chord.
This is a drawback to reconstruct near the boundary, but good for interior reconstruction.

