\section{conclusion}\label{sec:conclusion}
We present a first partial reconstruction result in the non-local vector tomography problem of recovering a planar vector field from its zero and first momenta ray transforms when data is only available on a strict subset of lines (the ones passing through an arc $\Lambda$).

 The reconstruction is based on solving  an inverse boundary value problem for a system of Bukhgeim-Beltrami equations  with partial data on a boundary arc $\Lambda$.
%We reduced the partial inversion of the  momenta Doppler transform of real valued vector field with data on part of boundary $\Lambda$, to an inverse  boundary value problem for a system of Bukhgeim-Beltrami equations  with partial data on $\Lambda$ 
%( see  \cite[Proposition 2.1.]{fujiwaraOmogbheSadiqTamasan23} and 
%\eqref{Beltrami_uk_sys} ).  
The key step is transporting the data from 
%boundary arc $\Lambda$ to the interior segment $L$
 $\Lambda$ to the inner chord $L$ (inaccessible by direct measurement) by solving an ill-posed Cauchy type singular integral equation. 

